-beta.14, when a compressed archive is uploaded to a container via `PUT /containers/{id}/archive` or piped through `docker cp -`, the daemon resolves decompression binaries (such as `xz` or `unpigz`) from the container's filesystem rather than the host's due to incorrect ordering of operations. A malicious container image containing a trojanized decompression binary can achieve arbitrary code execution with full daemon privileges, including host root UID and unrestricted capabilities, when a user uploads a compressed (xz or gzip) archive into that container. This issue is fixed in Docker Engine 29.5.1 and moby/moby v2.0.0-beta.14. Workarounds include only running containers from trusted images, using authorization plugins to restrict access to the `PUT /containers/{id}/archive` endpoint, and avoiding piping compressed archives into containers created from untrusted images","cvss":[{"source":"0b0ca135-0b70-47e7-9f44-1890c2a1c46c","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H","metrics":{"baseScore":7.5,"exploitabilityScore":0.9,"impactScore":6.1},"vendorMetadata":{}},{"source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary","version":"3.1","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:H/PR:L/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:N","metrics":{"baseScore":7.2,"exploitabilityScore":0.9,"impactScore":5.8},"vendorMetadata":{}}],"epss":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-41567","epss":0.00161,"percentile":0.05777,"date":"2026-08-15"}],"cwes":[{"cve":"CVE-2026-41567","cwe":"CWE-427","source":"security-advisories@github.com","type":"Secondary"},{"cve":"CVE-2026-41567","cwe":"CWE-427","source":"0b0ca135-0b70-47e7-9f44-1890c2a1c46c","type":"Secondary"}]}],"matchDetails":[{"type":"exact-direct-match","matcher":"go-module-matcher","searchedBy":{"language":"go","namespace":"github:language:go","package":{"name":"github.com/docker/docker","version":"v24.0.5+incompatible"}},"found":{"vulnerabilityID":"GHSA-x86f-5xw2-fm2r","versionConstraint":"<=28.5.2 (go)"}}],"artifact":{"id":"pkg:golang